WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.292
MARK MIRCHANDANI: Setting up
your Google Cloud Platform

00:00:02.292 --> 00:00:05.480
resources correctly can save you
a lot of trouble down the road.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.760
Let's look at how to manage
resources and the resource

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.130
hierarchy by adding
new resources,

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.975
managing permissions,
and creating labels.

00:00:11.975 --> 00:00:14.585
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.748
When setting up your resource
hierarchy in the GCP console,

00:00:22.748 --> 00:00:24.790
you'll need to be assigned
the right permissions,

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.190
such as the organization
administrator and folder

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.235
creator roles.

00:00:28.235 --> 00:00:30.610
This will ensure that you have
the right permissions when

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.440
setting up the initial
structure for your organization.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.100
But don't forget to go
back and review permissions

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.770
after you're set up to
ensure only the right people

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.900
can update your resources.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.730
The best place to
manage your resources

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.770
is on the resource
management page, which you

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.440
can find under IAM and Admin.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.110
This page shows all the
resources in an organization

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.455
and lets you manage them.

00:00:51.455 --> 00:00:53.080
Let's go through an
example of bringing

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.880
on a new line of business
to an organization.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.700
We'll start by adding
a folder directly

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.370
under the organization called
Department Y. To do this,

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.610
we can just click the Create
Folder button and type

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.330
in Department Y. A folder can
exist under the organization

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:11.278
or under another folder based
on your organization structure.

00:01:11.278 --> 00:01:13.570
For example, we could create
production and development

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.580
folders to help organize
your projects further

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.930
for each department.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.550
Since Department Y is
a new line of business,

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.300
we'll create it at the
organization level.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:26.850
Just like folders, when
we create a project,

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.762
we can choose a single
parent location,

00:01:28.762 --> 00:01:29.720
such as our new folder.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.200
Now that we have multiple
lines of business,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.760
our shared
infrastructure project

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.840
should probably
have its own folder.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.830
Let's create a new folder
called Shared Infrastructure.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.710
After that, we can move the
project under our new folder

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.120
by using the Options menu.

00:01:52.258 --> 00:01:54.550
Now our lines of business
and our shared infrastructure

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.080
have their own
independent folders.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.080
We can also manage
permissions on the right hand

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.613
side for the organization,
folders, and projects.

00:02:02.613 --> 00:02:04.780
Since we've just created a
new folder for our shared

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:07.870
infrastructure team, let's make
sure they have project creator

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:09.789
access to this new folder.

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:12.670
We can select the folder
and click Add Member.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.300
Let's add the shared infra group
and choose Project Creator.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.950
Now members of the
shared infra group

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.090
can create projects
under this folder.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.240
But it looks like everyone
else in the organization

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.468
can as well.

00:02:23.468 --> 00:02:25.510
That's because this
permission is being inherited

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:26.980
from the organization.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.350
We can use the toggle to see
which permissions have been

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.600
added directly or inherited.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.550
Since permissions are
inherited, folders

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:35.440
are also a good way
to organize projects

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.080
that have similar
permissions requirements.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.480
Google recommends a
least privilege approach.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.430
So you should only
grant access to those

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.122
who absolutely need it.

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:46.330
Let's go ahead and remove
the permission for everyone

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.330
in the org to create projects
by choosing the organization

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.460
and removing that permission.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.610
Other best practices include
using groups wherever possible

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.100
and to test permission
changes before making

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.450
the actual change.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.180
There's a link below
with more tips.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.740
Another way to
organize resources

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.810
is by adding labels,
which are key value

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.670
pairs that you can filter on.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.980
For example, it may make
sense to label projects

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.310
with a component.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.730
We'll select Department
X Prod and apply

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:17.860
a new label called Component
and set it to Dashboard.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.690
Other common uses
for labels include

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:22.390
distinguishing instances owned
by different call centers

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:23.860
or teams.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.880
As we've shown, the
resource management page

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.450
is a great place to see what
your organization looks like

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.250
and to mange your resources.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:33.780
Check out the links below
for more information.

